# PR screenshots

PRs that change `styles/`, `scripts/`, `chat/`, `includes/pages/**`, or any `*.tpl` must include a screenshot (CI `screenshot-check`). Bypass with the `skip-screenshot` label or `[skip-screenshot]` in the PR body plus a reason.

## Where screenshots go

- **Preferred:** upload the image in the PR body or a PR comment. GitHub hosts it under `user-attachments`.
- **Also fine:** attach screenshots as CI workflow artifacts with a short retention (e.g. `retention-days: 7`).
- **Never commit** review screenshots to the repository. Do not add files under `.pr-shots/` or `docs/review/`. Those paths are gitignored.

Link screenshots with markdown images (`![label](url)`) or `<img>` tags in the PR body so `screenshot-check` can see them. Do not use raw GitHub URLs that point at a branch or commit in this repo for review shots — those break when the branch is deleted.
